        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sin⁡x)=cos⁡x.$ Applying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5tan⁡x+2sin⁡x) \\\\  & =5{sec}^{2}⁡x+2cos⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =5{sec}^{2}⁡(0)+2cos⁡(0) \\\\  & =5+2(1) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $7.$",
